# AGENT CAPSULE

Bash hooks + local HANDOFF memory. One model per conversation.
Read `HANDOFF.md` for multi-session work. Prefer NO CODE. Smallest Diff.
Start: read HANDOFF.md tail. Stop with tools: update HANDOFF.
Git only when asked. Secrets never in code or chat.
Done = `docs/TOOLCHAIN.md` green with evidence.
Never fight a deny. Never reintroduce Rust kleos-gate or pack Python.

## Harness

Bash hooks: `session_start`, `before_submit_prompt`, `stop_gate`, `lean_gate`, `pre_tool_use` (+ `subagent_*`, `after_shell`, `before_read_file`, `session_end`). No Rust.
Brain = `HANDOFF.md` (local, always works).
Injection != Declaration: harness injects `additionalContext` only; user prompt is immutable. Never `updated_input`.

## INTENT protocol

Declare `INTENT:` as **chat prose before any tool** (never Shell/Write/code-fence — poisons stop detection).
Job card: `OBJECTIVE` = postcondition + `edit:path`|`NEW:path` tags; `CONSTRAINTS` ≤2 invariants; `Done-when` ≤5 decidable predicates.

## File map

Ground → tag → edit/NEW → re-Read → prove Done-when.
Glob/Grep/Read first; `StrReplace` existing; `Write` only NEW paths.
Finish EVERY tagged path this turn — no drip, no orphan unconnected files.
Before write: read `HANDOFF.md` for current session state.
Before Done: verify all Done-when predicates hold with evidence (build/test/curl/read).

## State

`/state/` overwrite-only; clears on stop_gate success.
`pending_files.md` survives stop followups until accept.
Law: `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` + `docs/CURATOR.md`.

## Autonomous loop (no early stops)

Work ends when every Done-when predicate holds — not after the first draft.

1. DECLARE FIRST: write INTENT in chat before any tool.
2. NO ASK INSIDE INTENT: missing Done-when work → do it now. Do not ask permission.
3. NO PARTIAL HANDOFFS / NO DRIP: ban "let me know…", "next pass", "will continue". Finish every tagged path this turn.
4. GROUND → TAG → EDIT: Glob/Grep/Read; tag `edit:path`|`NEW:path`; StrReplace existing; Write only NEW.
5. PRE-STOP: re-Read every tagged FILE; prove every Done-when predicate on disk/TOOLCHAIN; then `Done-when: met`.
6. CASCADE FIX: broken import/test from your change → fix same turn.
7. CLOSE: `Done-when: met` then stop. `stop_gate` reads **assistant prose only** and will followup on poison, drip, or unmet predicates.
